        "authorName": "null2264",
        "name": {
          "en-US": "Yōkai Nightly"
        },
        "description": {
          "en-US": "Nightly builds of Yōkai, the free and open source manga reader for\nAndroid. Rebuilt from the development branch on every upstream commit,\nso expect bugs that the stable releases do not have. Back up your\nlibrary before switching to a nightly and before updating it again.\n\nBecause this is a nightly, it is installed under its own package name\nnext to the stable app rather than replacing it. The two installs do\nnot share a database: a library built up in one is not visible in the\nother.\n\nFeatures are the same as the stable release: reading of downloaded\ncontent, local sources that read ComicInfo.xml, NSFW/SFW library\nfilters, multiple readers and reading directions, trackers for\nMyAnimeList, AniList, Kitsu, Manga Updates, Shikimori and Bangumi,\ncategories, backups and Material You themes.\n\nRequires Android 8.0 (API 26) or newer.\n\nExtensions are not part of this repository. They are downloaded from\nthe extension repository built into the app, and every source you add\ndetermines where the app connects to. Many of them are not free\nservices, which is why the app is tagged with the NonFreeNet\nanti-feature.\n\nThese builds are upstream's \"standard\" flavour, so they contain the\nproprietary Firebase and Google Play services libraries, hence the\nGooglePlay anti-feature. They are not builds from the F-Droid build\nservice.\n\nReport problems on the main repository, not on the nightly one:\nhttps://github.com/null2264/yokai/issues\n"
        },
