        "authorName": "null2264",
        "name": {
          "en-US": "Yōkai"
        },
        "description": {
          "en-US": "Yōkai is a free and open source manga reader for Android, forked from\nTachiyomi/Mihon. It ships without any content and only talks to the\nsources you install yourself, everything you download can be read\noffline afterwards.\n\nFeatures:\n\n• Reading of downloaded content, local sources read ComicInfo.xml for\nthe chapter title, number and scanlator.\n• NSFW/SFW library filters, categories and tags.\n• A configurable reader with multiple viewers, reading directions\nand per series settings.\n• Trackers for MyAnimeList, AniList, Kitsu, Manga Updates, Shikimori\nand Bangumi.\n• Scheduled library updates and local backups.\n• Material You themes, a staggered library grid, drag and drop\nsorting and dynamic categories.\n\nRequires Android 8.0 (API 26) or newer.\n\nExtensions are not part of this repository. They are downloaded from\nthe extension repository built into the app, and every source you add\ndetermines where the app connects to. Many of them are not free\nservices, which is why the app is tagged with the NonFreeNet\nanti-feature.\n\nThis build is upstream's \"standard\" flavour, so it contains the\nproprietary Firebase and Google Play services libraries, hence the\nGooglePlay anti-feature. It is not a build from the F-Droid build\nservice.\n"
        },
